# Saypy Collection — Deployment Guide

How to deploy the **backend** (`api/`, FastAPI + PostgreSQL) and the **frontend**
(`frontend/`, React + Vite) to a production server — first **without Docker**,
then **with Docker**.

> For running locally during development, see `how_to_run` (no Docker) and
> `DOCKER.md` (Docker dev stack). This file is only about production deployment.

---

## 0. Architecture & things to know first

```
            Browser
               │  https://collection.example.com
               ▼
        ┌──────────────┐
        │    nginx     │  :80 / :443  (TLS, static files, reverse proxy)
        └──────┬───────┘
     /         │          /api/*
 static SPA    │     ┌──────────────────────┐
 (dist/)       └────►│ FastAPI (uvicorn)    │ 127.0.0.1:8001
                     └──────────┬───────────┘
                                ▼
                     ┌──────────────────────┐
                     │ PostgreSQL           │ (not containerized)
                     └──────────────────────┘
```

Facts about this app that affect deployment:

| Topic | Detail |
|---|---|
| Backend port | `8001` (uvicorn, `app.main:app`) |
| Database | PostgreSQL. Schema comes **only** from Alembic (`alembic upgrade head`); there is no `create_all()` |
| Seed data | Runs automatically on **every** app start (`app/seed.py`), and it is safe to re-run. It creates the admin user and churches from `SEED_*` |
| Config | Backend reads `api/.env` (or real environment variables) |
| Encrypted secrets | `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET_KEY` and `SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD` may be stored as `enc:...`. They are decrypted with the key in `.secrets.key` at the repo root (or `ENV_SECRETS_KEY` / `ENV_SECRETS_KEY_FILE`) |
| Uploads | Evidence files are written to `api/uploads/`. **Back this directory up, and keep it across redeploys** |
| Frontend API URL | Set at **build time** by `VITE_API_BASE_URL` and `VITE_MEMBERS_API_BASE_URL`. If they are unset, the browser calls `<same-host>:8001` |
| Frontend routing | Client-side routes (`/dashboard`, `/self-register`, …), so the web server must fall back to `index.html` |
| Node version | Vite 7 needs **Node 20.19+ or 22.12+** |
| Python version | 3.12 (matches the Docker image) |

### Recommended production layout: one domain, `/api` proxied

Serve the frontend at `https://your-domain/` and proxy `https://your-domain/api/`
to the backend. Then build the frontend with:

```
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-domain/api
VITE_MEMBERS_API_BASE_URL=https://your-domain/api
```

Why: with HTTPS, the automatic `<host>:8001` fallback would call
`https://your-domain:8001`. That only works if port 8001 also serves TLS;
otherwise the browser blocks it as mixed content or a connection error. With
the proxy you need only one certificate and one open port (443), and port 8001
stays private.

Throughout this guide, replace:

- `collection.example.com` → your real domain (or the server IP if you have no domain)
- `saypy` / `STRONG_DB_PASSWORD` → your DB user and password
- `/opt/saypy-collection` → wherever you put the code

The commands assume **Ubuntu 22.04/24.04** (Debian works the same way) and a
user with `sudo`.

