# METHOD A — Deploy WITHOUT Docker

Stack: **systemd** runs uvicorn on `127.0.0.1:8001`; **nginx** serves the built
frontend and proxies `/api/` to the backend; **certbot** provides HTTPS.

## A.1 Install system packages

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y python3 python3-venv python3-pip git nginx curl build-essential libpq-dev

# Node.js 22 LTS (the Ubuntu default Node is too old for Vite 7)
curl -fsSL https://deb.nodesource.com/setup_22.x | sudo -E bash -
sudo apt install -y nodejs
node -v      # must be >= 20.19
python3 --version   # 3.12 recommended (3.11+ works)
```

## A.2 Create a service user

```bash
sudo useradd --system --create-home --home-dir /home/saypy --shell /usr/sbin/nologin saypy
sudo chown -R saypy:saypy /opt/saypy-collection
```
(Run later build/maintenance commands as this user with `sudo -u saypy ...`, or
temporarily give ownership back to yourself while building.)

## A.3 Backend: install

```bash
cd /opt/saypy-collection/api
sudo -u saypy python3 -m venv .venv
sudo -u saypy .venv/bin/pip install --upgrade pip
sudo -u saypy .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements.txt
sudo -u saypy mkdir -p uploads
```

## A.4 Backend: configure `api/.env`

```bash
sudo -u saypy cp .env.example .env
sudo -u saypy nano .env
```

Production values:
```ini
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://saypy:STRONG_DB_PASSWORD@localhost:5432/saypy_core
# or: DATABASE_URL=enc:gAAAAAB...

JWT_SECRET_KEY=<long random value from step 1.4>
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
JWT_EXPIRE_MINUTES=480

# Lock CORS to your real frontend origin (comma-separate several)
CORS_ORIGINS=https://collection.example.com

SEED_ADMIN_USERNAME=admin
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=<strong initial password>
SEED_CHURCH_NAMES=Kibada,KCC,Mwera,Goroka
```

```bash
sudo chmod 600 /opt/saypy-collection/api/.env
```

If you used `enc:` values, the key at `/opt/saypy-collection/.secrets.key` is
found automatically. If you keep it somewhere else, set
`ENV_SECRETS_KEY_FILE=/path/to/key` in the systemd unit below.

## A.5 Backend: run migrations

```bash
cd /opt/saypy-collection/api
sudo -u saypy .venv/bin/alembic upgrade head
```

Quick smoke test (Ctrl+C to stop):
```bash
sudo -u saypy .venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001
# in another terminal:
curl http://127.0.0.1:8001/health
```

## A.6 Backend: systemd service

Create `/etc/systemd/system/saypy-api.service`:
```ini
[Unit]
Description=Saypy Collection API (FastAPI/uvicorn)
After=network.target postgresql.service
Wants=postgresql.service

[Service]
User=saypy
Group=saypy
WorkingDirectory=/opt/saypy-collection/api
# Uncomment if .secrets.key isn't at the repo root:
# Environment=ENV_SECRETS_KEY_FILE=/etc/saypy/.secrets.key
ExecStartPre=/opt/saypy-collection/api/.venv/bin/alembic upgrade head
ExecStart=/opt/saypy-collection/api/.venv/bin/uvicorn app.main:app \
    --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8001 --workers 4 \
    --proxy-headers --forwarded-allow-ips=127.0.0.1
Restart=always
RestartSec=5

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable --now saypy-api
sudo systemctl status saypy-api
journalctl -u saypy-api -f        # live logs
```

`ExecStartPre` applies any new migrations on every restart, the same way the
Docker entrypoint does.

## A.7 Frontend: build

```bash
cd /opt/saypy-collection/frontend
sudo -u saypy npm ci

# Bake the public API URL into the bundle (see section 0)
sudo -u saypy env \
  VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://collection.example.com/api \
  VITE_MEMBERS_API_BASE_URL=https://collection.example.com/api \
  npm run build
```

You can put these two variables in `frontend/.env.production` instead; Vite
picks that file up automatically during `npm run build`.

Publish the build:
```bash
sudo mkdir -p /var/www/saypy
sudo rsync -a --delete /opt/saypy-collection/frontend/dist/ /var/www/saypy/
sudo chown -R www-data:www-data /var/www/saypy
```

## A.8 nginx

Create `/etc/nginx/sites-available/saypy`:
```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name collection.example.com;

    # Collection imports (Excel) and evidence uploads
    client_max_body_size 25M;

    root /var/www/saypy;
    index index.html;

    # API — strip the /api prefix (the FastAPI routes are mounted at /)
    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8001/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host              $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;   # long reports/imports
    }

    # Fingerprinted assets: cache aggressively
    location /assets/ {
        expires 30d;
        access_log off;
        try_files $uri =404;
    }

    # SPA fallback for client-side routes
    location / {
        try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
    }
}
```

The trailing `/` in `proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8001/;` matters: it makes
`/api/auth/login` reach the backend as `/auth/login`.

```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/saypy /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo rm -f /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/default
sudo nginx -t && sudo systemctl reload nginx
```

## A.9 HTTPS (Let's Encrypt)

```bash
sudo apt install -y certbot python3-certbot-nginx
sudo certbot --nginx -d collection.example.com --redirect
sudo certbot renew --dry-run     # check that auto-renewal works
```

## A.10 Firewall

```bash
sudo ufw allow OpenSSH
sudo ufw allow 'Nginx Full'     # 80 + 443
sudo ufw enable
```
Do **not** open 8001 or 5432. The backend and Postgres are only reached
locally.

## A.11 Verify

1. `curl https://collection.example.com/api/health` returns OK.
2. Open `https://collection.example.com` and log in as `admin` with
   `SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD`.
3. **Change the admin password immediately** (User Management → Reset Password).
4. Hard-refresh a deep link such as `/dashboard`. It should load, not show a 404.
5. Upload an evidence file and confirm it appears under `api/uploads/`.

## A.12 Updating (redeploy)

```bash
cd /opt/saypy-collection
sudo -u saypy git pull

# Backend
sudo -u saypy api/.venv/bin/pip install -r api/requirements.txt
sudo systemctl restart saypy-api          # runs alembic upgrade head first

# Frontend
cd frontend
sudo -u saypy npm ci
sudo -u saypy npm run build               # uses frontend/.env.production if you created it
sudo rsync -a --delete dist/ /var/www/saypy/
```

## A.13 Alternative: no domain, no proxy (LAN / quick setup)

If you deploy on a LAN by IP without HTTPS, you can skip `/api` proxying and use
the built-in fallback:

- Run uvicorn with `--host 0.0.0.0 --port 8001` and open port 8001 in the firewall.
- Build the frontend with **no** `VITE_*` variables.
- Serve `dist/` with nginx on port 80 (same config as above without the
  `location /api/` block).

The browser then calls `http://<server-ip>:8001` automatically. Don't use
this setup over the public internet.

