## C. Backups (both methods)

Back up two things: **the database** and **`api/uploads/`**.

```bash
# /etc/cron.daily/saypy-backup   (chmod +x)
#!/bin/sh
set -e
DEST=/var/backups/saypy
mkdir -p "$DEST"
STAMP=$(date +%F)
PGPASSWORD='STRONG_DB_PASSWORD' pg_dump -h localhost -U saypy -Fc saypy_core > "$DEST/saypy_core_$STAMP.dump"
tar -czf "$DEST/uploads_$STAMP.tar.gz" -C /opt/saypy-collection/api uploads
find "$DEST" -type f -mtime +14 -delete     # keep 14 days
```

Restore:
```bash
pg_restore -h localhost -U saypy -d saypy_core --clean --no-owner saypy_core_YYYY-MM-DD.dump
tar -xzf uploads_YYYY-MM-DD.tar.gz -C /opt/saypy-collection/api
```

Copy backups off the server too (rsync, S3, etc.). Also keep `.secrets.key` and
the env files in a password manager.

